# Tokenizer files that save_pretrained copies next to a trained adapter.
# They are byte-identical to microsoft/unixcoder-base's own, and nothing
# reloads them from here: the pipelines always build the tokenizer with
# AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME), and PeftModel.from_pretrained
# reads only adapter_config.json and adapter_model.safetensors. Keeping them
# added ~5 MB of duplicated vocabulary to every clone.
model_lora/tokenizer.json
model_lora/tokenizer_config.json
model_lora/special_tokens_map.json
model_lora/vocab.json
model_lora/merges.txt

# The full finetune writes a complete 126M-parameter checkpoint. That is far
# too large for git; it belongs in the Zenodo deposit if it is published at
# all. The LoRA adapter is small enough to track and is the one people will
# actually reuse.
model_st/
